  "question": {
    "text": "Let the complex numbers <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">α</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mfrac></math> lie on the circles <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi><mo>-</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi><mo>-</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></math> respectively, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></math>. Then, the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>|</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">α</mi><msup><mo>|</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></math> is__________.",
